# precedent environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in what you need.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit a real key to this repository.
# Everything here is optional except FAC_API_KEY, and FAC_API_KEY is only
# needed for the pass-through commands. The award history commands work with
# no credentials at all.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FAC_API_KEY  (required for `precedent passthrough` and `precedent recipient`)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Federal Audit Clearinghouse API key. This unlocks single audit data and the
# Schedule of Expenditures of Federal Awards, which is what the pass-through
# finder reads.
#
# Where to get it:
#   1. Go to https://www.fac.gov/api/signup/
#   2. Enter your name and email address. That is the entire process.
#   3. The key arrives by email from api.data.gov, usually within a minute.
#
# Cost: free. No account, no approval queue, no credit card, no usage tier
# to choose. It is an api.data.gov key, so it is rate limited per key rather
# than per IP address.
#
# How precedent sends it: as an `X-Api-Key` header on requests to
# https://api.fac.gov/. See docs/research/data-sources.md.
#
# Terms of use, worth reading before you redistribute derived data:
#   https://www.fac.gov/api/terms/
#
FAC_API_KEY=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENGRANTS_API_KEY  (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Adds a live enrichment layer showing the currently open funding
# opportunities under a program, alongside its historical awardee profile.
#
# precedent is fully functional without this. If the key is absent, expired,
# or the network is unavailable, commands return their complete public-data
# result and simply omit the enrichment section. Nothing degrades and nothing
# nags.
#
# Where to get it:
#   1. Sign in at https://opengrants.io
#   2. Open the Developer Dashboard and create an API key.
#   3. Free search is unlimited without an account; the paid tier is $9/month
#      at the time of writing. Confirm current pricing on the site.
#
# Docs: https://ops.opengrants.io/api-docs
# Hosted MCP server: https://mcp.opengrants.io/mcp
#
OPENGRANTS_API_KEY=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional tuning. Sensible defaults are built in; you rarely need these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where cached upstream responses are stored.
# Default: the platform cache directory, for example
# ~/.cache/precedent on Linux.
# PRECEDENT_CACHE_DIR=

# Cache lifetime overrides, in hours. Defaults are chosen to match how often
# each upstream actually changes, not to be aggressive for its own sake.
#   USAspending: 168 hours (7 days)
#   FAC:         168 hours (7 days; FAC production refreshes weekly, typically
#                Wednesdays)
#   OpenGrants:   24 hours
# PRECEDENT_CACHE_TTL_USASPENDING_HOURS=168
# PRECEDENT_CACHE_TTL_FAC_HOURS=168
# PRECEDENT_CACHE_TTL_OPENGRANTS_HOURS=24

# Set to 1 to bypass the cache entirely for one run. Equivalent to --no-cache.
# PRECEDENT_NO_CACHE=

# Contact string appended to the User-Agent header sent to public APIs, so
# operators can reach you if your usage causes a problem. Being a good
# citizen of free public infrastructure is a requirement of this project.
# PRECEDENT_CONTACT=you@example.org
